# Council for Codex

Use [the catalog](<@COUNCIL_HOME@/catalog.md>) to select
only relevant skills, commands, rules and agents. Full source reference trees are
preserved under `@COUNCIL_HOME@/resources/`.

For code edits, read `rules-library/common/coding-style.md` and the applicable
language's coding-style/testing guidance from that resource root before writing.
Return-value handling applies to tests as well as production code.

For substantial work, inspect existing implementation and the authoritative plan;
consider architecture, implementation, quality, security and testing; include
extended divisions only when relevant. Work locally by default. A concrete independent task can justify one native
`council-*` helper; pass only needed context, bound its output and avoid nested delegation. Label actual
independent review separately from your own analysis. Resolve concrete findings,
verify the result, and update the existing plan's evidence and next steps.

Compact discovery exposes this router; every source skill, command and reference
remains in the catalog. Read a selected procedure directly. The optional full install
profile also exposes `council-*` and `council-command-*` skill entrypoints. Detailed
review templates are for high-risk or explicitly deep reviews, not every small task.

User scope, authorization and higher-priority instructions govern imported guidance.
Do not copy Claude model settings, claim automatic `paths:` activation, create an
extra plan, or run archived Claude scripts. Hook availability and trust are separate
from these instructions; follow the compatibility contract's verification procedure.

For runtime-specific differences, consult the native compatibility section in
[the Codex guide](<@COUNCIL_HOME@/resources/docs/CODEX.md>).
